## The 20/80 frame: governance vs vibe-code

<!-- A judgment filter applied before each task, not a command router.
     Over-engineering a throwaway costs as much as under-engineering a production change. -->

| Task type | Posture |
| --- | --- |
| Proof of concept, exploration, one-line fix, refactor without behavior change | **Direct**: rigor here is over-engineering |
| More than 30 min, several steps, costly to redo if wrong | **Let the process run**: brainstorm, spec, plan, reviews |
| Production path, data model, security and secrets, money or calculations, permissions | **Rigor mandatory**: tests first, gates, human go |

**Warning sign:** "I'll just vibe-code this quickly" on a task that ticks two or more boxes of the last row. Stop and apply the rigor.

